+// RENORM_SHIFT[range_m1] is the number of bits to shift the entropy coder
+// state by, when decoder.read_bit reads an entropy coded bit, so that range_m1
+// stays in the range [0x7F ..= 0xFE].
+//
+// It is a look-up table for:
+//
+// RENORM_SHIFT[range_m1] = 7 - log2(range_m1 + 1)
+//
+// Equivalently:
+//
+// RENORM_SHIFT[range_m1] = 24 ^ __builtin_clz((uint32_t)(range_m1 + 1))
+//
+// Note that the final (255th) element is unused.
+//
+// If range_m1 >= 0x7F then RENORM_SHIFT[range_m1] is zero, so that shifting or
